格式示例（仅结构，不是来源事实）：evidence:[{"paragraph_id":"p3s1","fact":"该片段支持的中文转述"}]。请从本次真实输入挑选编号。","role":"system"},{"content":"{"metadata":{"description":"DeepSeek Harness (DSH) backup & restore plugin — export, import, migrate and sync your complete DSH configuration, plugins, MCP servers, skills and workspace. One-click migration to another machine.","id":"gh:1334434081","install_available":true,"language":"TypeScript","name":"dsh-config-manager","slug":"xiajiajun516/dsh-config-manager","topics":["backup","cli","config-manager","configuration","cordis","deepseek","deepseek-harness","dsh","dsh-plugin","export","import","mcp","migration","plugin","restore","settings","skills","sync","webdav","workspace"]},"paragraphs":[{"id":"p1s1","text":"DeepSeek Harness (DSH) backup & restore plugin — export, import, migrate and sync your complete DSH "},{"id":"p1s2","text":"configuration, plugins, MCP servers, skills and workspace. One-click migration to another machine."},{"id":"p2s1","text":"# 🎒 DSH Config Manager"},{"id":"p3s1","text":"**DeepSeek Harness Backup, Restore & Migration Plugin.**"},{"id":"p4s1","text":"Backup, restore, export, import, migrate and sync your complete DeepSeek Harness (DSH) configuration"},{"id":"p4s2","text":" — settings, model providers, plugins, MCP servers, skills, agent presets and workspaces — and resto"},{"id":"p4s3","text":"re your whole environment on a new machine with one click."},{"id":"p5s1","text":"- 🔄 **Backup & Restore** DeepSeek Harness configuration\n- 📦 **Export / Import** complete DSH configu"},{"id":"p5s2","text":"ration\n- 🚚 **Migrate** DSH to another machine\n- ⏰ **Scheduled full backups** — automatic, on your ow"},{"id":"p5s3","text":"n cadence (6h / 12h / 24h / 7d / custom weekly), secrets never included\n- 🔌 Backup installed **plugi"},{"id":"p5s4","text":"ns** and plugin configuration\n- 🧩 Backup **MCP servers** and **Skills**\n- 🔐 Encrypted backups with o"},{"id":"p5s5","text":"ptional credentials\n- ☁️ **Git / WebDAV** configuration sync\n- 🛒 **Configuration market** — browse &"},{"id":"p5s6","text":" one-click install shared configs\n- 🧳 **Import from other AI agents** — Claude Code, Cursor, Codex, "},{"id":"p5s7","text":"Hermes, Antigravity … config **and chat history**\n- ↩️ Automatic snapshot and rollback before restor"},{"id":"p5s8","text":"ermes, Antigravity … config **and chat history**\n- ↩️ Automatic snapshot and rollback before restore"},{"id":"p6s1","text":"English · 简体中文"},{"id":"p7s1","text":"## What is this? 🤔"},{"id":"p8s1","text":"DSH is your AI assistant workbench — it holds your settings: model configs, plugins, skills, workspa"},{"id":"p8s2","text":"is your AI assistant workbench — it holds your settings: model configs, plugins, skills, workspaces…"},{"id":"p9s1","text":"**DSH Config Manager is its \"moving service\"**:"},{"id":"p10s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p11s1","text":"> ⚠️ **Security first**: no secrets (API Key / Token / Password) are exported by default. See Securi"},{"id":"p11s2","text":"️ **Security first**: no secrets (API Key / Token / Password) are exported by default. See Security."},{"id":"p12s1","text":"## 🎯 Use Cases"},{"id":"p13s1","text":"### Backup DeepSeek Harness configuration"},{"id":"p14s1","text":"Create a portable backup of your DSH settings, model providers, plugins, MCP servers, skills, agent "},{"id":"p14s2","text":"presets and workspace — one ZIP file, no secret values included by default. (DSH's own profiles — `$"},{"id":"p14s3","text":"DSH_HOME/profiles/<name>`, i.e. which plugin stack to boot — are machine-local and are **not** part "},{"id":"p14s4","text":"of the backup; the **Environment → Profiles** view manages them instead — list / create / rename / d"},{"id":"p14s5","text":"elete, plus launching or stopping an independent instance for one.)"},{"id":"p15s1","text":"### Restore DeepSeek Harness on another machine"},{"id":"p16s1","text":"Export your current DSH environment as a single ZIP and import it on a new Windows, macOS or Linux m"},{"id":"p16s2","text":"achine. One click brings back settings, plugins, MCP servers, skills and global instructions (AGENTS"},{"id":"p16s3","text":"e. One click brings back settings, plugins, MCP servers, skills and global instructions (AGENTS.md)."},{"id":"p17s1","text":"### Migrate DSH configuration to a new computer"},{"id":"p18s1","text":"Move your complete DeepSeek Harness setup without manually reinstalling plugins, MCP servers and ski"},{"id":"p18s2","text":"lls. Dead absolute paths are detected and remapped automatically (batch prefix mapping supported)."},{"id":"p19s1","text":"### Sync DSH configuration across machines"},{"id":"p20s1","text":"[该节后续省略]"},{"id":"p21s1","text":"## 🔄 How it works?"},{"id":"p22s1","text":"## 🧩 Features"},{"id":"p23s1","text":"## 🛡️ Security"},{"id":"p24s1","text":"- **The default backup contains no secret values** — a hard invariant, enforced at export\n- **Not ex"},{"id":"p24s2","text":"ported by default**: API Keys / passwords / tokens / cookies / sessions / device unique ID / logs & "},{"id":"p24s3","text":"cache / plugin binaries\n- **A ZIP is untrusted input**: defends against Zip Slip, malicious paths, z"},{"id":"p24s4","text":"ip bombs, corrupt archives — any trigger rejects the whole file\n- **Logs are fully redacted** — secr"},{"id":"p24s5","text":"et values never reach logs\n- **Encrypted backup (explicit opt-in)**: secrets are exported only as sc"},{"id":"p24s6","text":"rypt + AES-256-GCM ciphertext — random salt & IV per export, never plaintext; the password lives in "},{"id":"p24s7","text":"256-GCM ciphertext — random salt & IV per export, never plaintext; the password lives in memory only"},{"id":"p25s1","text":"## 🤝 Compatibility"},{"id":"p26s1","text":"| Status | Meaning |"},{"id":"p27s1","text":"| ✅ Excellent | Same platform, complete sections, supported schema |\n| 👍 Good | Backup from an older"},{"id":"p27s2","text":" DSH |\n| ⚠️ Partial | Cross-platform / missing sections / backup newer than target |\n| ❌ Unsupported"},{"id":"p27s3","text":" | Schema beyond the supported range (cannot import) |"},{"id":"p28s1","text":"## 📋 Known limitations (user-facing)"},{"id":"p29s1","text":"1. **Installing / updating plugins or MCP takes effect after restarting DSH**\n2. **Some UI state is "},{"id":"p29s2","text":"not migrated** (e.g. task board data, panel widths — they live in the browser, not in DSH's config f"},{"id":"p29s3","text":"iles)\n3. **keybindings / workflow configs / commands** — DSH has no such concepts, so nothing is exp"},{"id":"p29s4","text":"orted for them. Global agent rules are covered by **Agent Instructions** (`~/.dsh/AGENTS.md`, inject"},{"id":"p29s5","text":"ed into every session); per-project `AGENTS.md`/`CLAUDE.md` belong to each project's repo and are no"},{"id":"p29s6","text":"t migrated\n4. **History/session migration is opt-in** — DSH's own sessions are only exported/synced "},{"id":"p29s7","text":"when you explicitly select the `sessions` section (the sync channel additionally needs both sides to"},{"id":"p29s8","text":" allow it); **MCP servers are the other opt-in sync section** — the `mcp` section is `platformSpecif"},{"id":"p29s9","text":"ic`, so it is never in the default sync set; tick **MCP Servers** in the sync-section dialog to carr"},{"id":"p29s10","text":"y it (auto sync follows along, but a pulled `mcp` change still lands in the diff review, since it is"},{"id":"p29s11","text":" a medium-risk section). Servers whose `command` / `cwd` are absolute paths, or whose runtime (npx /"},{"id":"p29s12","text":" uvx / pipx) is missing on the target, are reported by the import analysis — the config is written a"},{"id":"p29s13","text":"nyway; **another agent's chat history is migrated when you pick that source** in the foreign import."},{"id":"p29s14","text":" Conversation state that DSH's session format has no room for (model reasoning traces, images, compa"},{"id":"p29s15","text":"ction checkpoints) is counted and reported, never fabricated\n5. **Encrypted backups**: a lost passwo"},{"id":"p29s16","text":"rd means the `secrets.enc` can't be decrypted (by design — keep your password safe)\n6. **Snapshot re"},{"id":"p29s17","text":"store is offline and honest**: entries the offline engine can't restore (settings namespaces / patch"},{"id":"p29s18","text":" lines when the snapshot has no whole-file backup, workspace records stored in DSH storages) are rep"},{"id":"p29s19","text":"orted as skipped with a pointer to online rollback; credential **values** are never auto-written (ma"},{"id":"p29s20","text":"nual re-entry hint only); old snapshots without a plugin baseline only get a hint to remove added pl"},{"id":"p29s21","text":"ugins manually\n[该节后续省略]"}],"truncated":true}","role":"user"}],"model":"MiniMax-M3.1-Flash","reasoning_effort":"low","stream":false}
